[ledge] Wrong build direction for this factory tool. magnet-retention.md specifies the common Y76.515 back on the bed, with machine +Y as build-up. These Z-normal bridge faces are vertical in that pose. The hash-bound factory_gauge_build_pose_review in magnet-geometry.json reads the canonical STL and finds every horizontal print-down facet on the bed.
alternatives: Printing upright in machine +Z would require support below both bridge arms. The specified flat-back pose retains the required 1.754 mm pole-setting step, with the central rib, both feet and bridge starting directly on the common bed plane; changing the gauge's machine-frame geometry is unnecessary.
