[thin] Wrong threshold classification at the nominal 3 mm boundary. The tool plate is exactly 3.000 mm between Y76.515 and Y79.515. The canonical STL's corresponding coordinate interval also measures exactly 3.000 mm, meeting the ordinary wall dimension. The gauge_three_mm_boundary_review in magnet-geometry.json binds both surfaces and their hashes.
alternatives: Adding a small thickness solely to move an exact 3 mm plate past the classifier's numeric boundary changes the factory tool without addressing an actual thin section. The classifier should distinguish its numeric threshold from a material section below 3 mm; printed gauge accuracy remains a separate measurement.
